Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 13:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Kompakt: turning auto brightness off forgets the slider point

A slider change while auto brightness is on is kept as a user point in
the short term model, which stock only invalidates five minutes after
the screen goes off. Turning auto off and on again therefore came back
at the adjusted curve, not the configured one. The point is now reset
when the setting goes to manual, so auto on starts from the curve.
---
diff --git a/services/core/java/com/android/server/display/DisplayPowerController.java b/services/core/java/com/android/server/display/DisplayPowerController.java
--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/display/DisplayPowerController.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/display/DisplayPowerController.java
@@ -2578,6 +2578,10 @@
         if (screenBrightnessModeSetting == Settings.System.SCREEN_BRIGHTNESS_MODE_MANUAL) {
             // In manual mode, all brightness changes should be saved immediately.
             mDisplayBrightnessController.saveBrightnessIfNeeded();
+            // Kompakt: auto off forgets the slider point, so auto on starts from the curve.
+            if (mAutomaticBrightnessController != null) {
+                mAutomaticBrightnessController.resetShortTermModel();
+            }
         }
     }
 
